# ==============================================================================
# llama-native-tools/.gitignore
# ==============================================================================
#
# LINE 1 IS LOAD-BEARING - DO NOT DELETE IT.
#
# The repository-root .gitignore is the standard Visual Studio / .NET one. It
# ignores directory and file names that also occur inside the vendored
# llama.cpp source tree, for example:
#
#     [Aa][Rr][Mm]/      -> llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/arm/
#     [Oo]ut/  [Ll][Oo][Gg]/  [Rr]elease/  [Dd]ebug/  bld/  [Oo]bj/  *.env ...
#
# Without the "!*" below, those folders would be silently left out of every
# commit, and the vendored snapshot would not build for the next person who
# cloned this repository. A nested .gitignore takes precedence over the ones
# above it, so re-including everything here and then re-ignoring only what this
# folder genuinely produces is the correct fix - and it keeps the root
# .gitignore untouched.
#
# Verify at any time with:
#     git check-ignore -v llama-native-tools/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/arm/quants.c
#     git check-ignore -v llama-native-tools/linux/pins.env
#         -> both should print nothing (i.e. the files are NOT ignored)
# ==============================================================================

# Re-include everything under this folder, overriding the root .gitignore.
!*
!*/

# --- what this folder really does produce, and must not commit ---------------

# Built native libraries, unstripped copies, dSYM bundles, staged archives,
# BUILD-INFO files. ONE tree, shared by all three platform builds, so all seven
# RIDs land side by side.
#
# THE LEADING SLASH MATTERS. Without it this pattern would match ANY directory
# named "output" at any depth inside the vendored tree.
# NOTE THE TRAILING /* RATHER THAN A BARE /output/. A directory that is itself
# excluded is never descended into, so a later "!" rule can NEVER re-include a
# file inside it. Excluding the CONTENTS leaves the directory visible, and the
# negation below then works.
/output/*

# ...except the placeholder README that explains what goes there.
!/output/README.txt

# Local scratch that the scripts may leave behind.
*.tmp
*.log
build-scratch/

# Finder droppings. Needed explicitly: the "!*" above re-includes everything
# under this folder and so overrides any .DS_Store rule inherited from the root
# or from a user's global gitignore.
.DS_Store
